= Computer architecture — Simple =

'''Computer architecture''' is the structure of a computer system and the rules software uses to control it.

It includes things such as:

* what instructions the processor understands;
* how memory is organized;
* how data moves;
* how input and output work;
* how several operations can happen in parallel.

The instruction set is the part software can directly target.

Two processors can use the same instruction set while having very different internal designs.

That internal implementation is called microarchitecture.

